{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/transfer_peer.cljd; nl -ba test/yin/vm/linker/remote_transfer_test.cljc | sed -n '224,360p'; rg -n '5a|10\\\\.|4.5|B0|cross.host|remote transfer' docs/design/yin.vm.linker-spec.md docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md; git status --short; git diff eed6c63c --stat\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns yin.vm.linker.transfer-peer\n     2\t  \"Dart receiver for the JVM transfer test. Bootstrap contains only\n     3\t   format, identity, and index. Transit lines carry remote protocol\n     4\t   envelopes; each side interprets them through dao.stream.remote over\n     5\t   rings. Verified H and R images execute in their native VMs.\"\n     6\t  (:require [\"dart:io\" :as io]\n     7\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n     8\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]\n     9\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ring]\n    10\t            [dao.stream.transit :as transit]\n    11\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n    12\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    13\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    14\t            [yin.vm.linker :as linker]))\n    15\t\n    16\t\n    17\t(defn- medium\n    18\t  []\n    19\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n    20\t    (ring/create! {:dao.stream/type ring/transport-type\n    21\t                   ring/capacity-key 256})))\n    22\t\n    23\t\n    24\t(defn- emit!\n    25\t  [value]\n    26\t  (.writeln ^io/Stdout io/stdout (transit/encode value)))\n    27\t\n    28\t\n    29\t(defn- read!\n    30\t  []\n    31\t  (transit/decode (.readLineSync ^io/Stdin io/stdin)))\n    32\t\n    33\t\n    34\t(defn- drain!\n    35\t  [handle cursor]\n    36\t  (loop [values []]\n    37\t    (let [r (stream/next handle @cursor)]\n    38\t      (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    39\t        (do (reset! cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n    40\t            (recur (conj values (:dao.stream/value r))))\n    41\t        values))))\n    42\t\n    43\t\n    44\t(defn ^{:dart/name main} main\n    45\t  [_args]\n    46\t  (let [{:keys [kind identity index]} (read!)\n    47\t        format (case kind :H linker/stack-format :R linker/register-format)\n    48\t        load-image (case kind :H dvm/create-vm :R rvm/create-vm)\n    49\t        incoming (medium)\n    50\t        outgoing (medium)\n    51\t        cursor (atom (:dao.stream/cursor\n    52\t                       (stream/cursor outgoing :dao.stream/oldest)))\n    53\t        channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.test/channel\n    54\t                 :dao.stream/identity \"jvm-dart-linker\"}\n    55\t        attach! (remote/attacher\n    56\t                  {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n    57\t                   {channel {:reader incoming :writer outgoing}}})\n    58\t        attach (fn [name]\n    59\t                 (:dao.stream/handle\n    60\t                   (attach! {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n    61\t                             :dao.stream/identity name\n    62\t                             :dao.stream/channel channel})))\n    63\t        runtime {:state (linker/link-state\n    64\t                          {:formats {(:format format) format}\n    65\t                           :indexes {(:format format) index}\n    66\t                           :content {:requests (attach \"requests\")\n    67\t                                     :answers (attach \"answers\")\n    68\t                                     :cursor :dao.stream/newest}})\n    69\t                 :drive (fn [state]\n    70\t                          (emit! {:wire (drain! outgoing cursor)})\n    71\t                          (doseq [value (:wire (read!))]\n    72\t                            (stream/append! incoming value))\n    73\t                          state)}\n    74\t        result (linker/fetch runtime (:format format) identity\n    75\t                             {:primitives vm/primitives}\n    76\t                             {:contract (:contract format)})]\n    77\t    (emit!\n    78\t      (if (linker/ok? result)\n    79\t        {:result (dissoc result :value)\n    80\t         :identity-matches\n    81\t         ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity (:value result))\n    82\t         :value (vm/value\n    83\t                  (vm/run\n    84\t                    (load-image (:value result)\n    85\t                                {:primitives vm/primitives\n    86\t                                 :contract (:contract format)})))}\n    87\t        {:result result}))))\n   224\t(deftest an-image-transfers-to-a-receiver-holding-identity-and-index\n   225\t  (doseq [[label format mint lift] pinned-formats]\n   226\t    (testing label\n   227\t      (let [pub (publisher-leg)\n   228\t            image (mint worked-example)\n   229\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish pub format image)\n   230\t            res (linker/fetch (receiver-leg pub format index)\n   231\t                              (:format format) identity receiver-env\n   232\t                              (requested format))]\n   233\t        (is (linker/ok? res) (pr-str res))\n   234\t        (is (= (:format format) (:format res)))\n   235\t        (is (= identity (:identity res)))\n   236\t        (is (= (get index identity) (:address res)))\n   237\t        (is (= image (:value res))\n   238\t            \"the image the publisher minted is the image received\")\n   239\t        (is (= '[+] (mapv :name (:obligations res)))\n   240\t            \"the free `+` is the image's one retained obligation\")\n   241\t        (is (= (named-value worked-example)\n   242\t               (lifted-value (lift (:value res))))\n   243\t            \"lifted, the transferred image runs under the semantic VM\n   244\t             B0-equal to the local evaluation\")\n   245\t        (jing/close! (:store pub))))))\n   246\t\n   247\t\n   248\t;; =============================================================================\n   249\t;; Criterion 6 and 5c: the refusals over the same channel\n   250\t;; =============================================================================\n   251\t\n   252\t(deftest a-swapped-identity-is-refused-over-the-stream\n   253\t  (doseq [[label format mint _lift] pinned-formats]\n   254\t    (testing label\n   255\t      (let [pub (publisher-leg)\n   256\t            wanted ((:identity-fn format) (mint worked-example))\n   257\t            [actual _attr address] (linker/publish! (:store pub) format\n   258\t                                                    (mint other-program))\n   259\t            index {wanted address}\n   260\t            res (linker/fetch (receiver-leg pub format index)\n   261\t                              (:format format) wanted receiver-env\n   262\t                              (requested format))]\n   263\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :hash-mismatch,\n   264\t                :expected wanted, :actual actual}\n   265\t               res)\n   266\t            \"the index's claim is checked, never trusted: the address\n   267\t             served, the identity refused\")\n   268\t        (jing/close! (:store pub))))))\n   269\t\n   270\t\n   271\t(defn- corrupting\n   272\t  \"The store answering every read it holds with corrupted bytes: the\n   273\t   canonical bytes of another value, which no longer hash to the\n   274\t   address they are served under.\"\n   275\t  [store]\n   276\t  (assoc store\n   277\t         :get-bytes-fn\n   278\t         (fn [address not-found]\n   279\t           (let [x ((:get-bytes-fn store) address not-found)]\n   280\t             (if (identical? x not-found)\n   281\t               x\n   282\t               (jing/canonical-bytes [:tampered (cbor/decode x)]))))))\n   283\t\n   284\t\n   285\t(deftest a-corrupt-payload-is-refused-over-the-stream\n   286\t  (doseq [[label format mint _lift] pinned-formats]\n   287\t    (testing label\n   288\t      (let [pub (publisher-leg)\n   289\t            image (mint worked-example)\n   290\t            {:keys [identity index]} (publish pub format image)\n   291\t            corrupt (assoc pub :store (corrupting (:store pub)))\n   292\t            res (linker/fetch (receiver-leg corrupt format index)\n   293\t                              (:format format) identity receiver-env\n   294\t                              (requested format))]\n   295\t        (is (= :address-mismatch (:reason res)) (pr-str res))\n   296\t        (is (= (get index identity) (:address res)))\n   297\t        (is (not (contains? res :value))\n   298\t            \"mismatched bytes are refused undecoded\")\n   299\t        (jing/close! (:store pub))))))\n   300\t\n   301\t\n   302\t(deftest an-address-the-publisher-lacks-is-absent-over-the-stream\n   303\t  (doseq [[label format mint _lift] pinned-formats]\n   304\t    (testing label\n   305\t      (let [pub (publisher-leg)\n   306\t            identity ((:identity-fn format) (mint worked-example))\n   307\t            index {identity (jing/segment-key [:none])}\n   308\t            res (linker/fetch (receiver-leg pub format index)\n   309\t                              (:format format) identity receiver-env\n   310\t                              (requested format))]\n   311\t        (is (= {:status :refused, :reason :absent,\n   312\t                :address (jing/segment-key [:none])}\n   313\t               res)\n   314\t            \"not found on the stream is the linker's :absent\")\n   315\t        (jing/close! (:store pub))))))\nrg: docs/design/yin.vm.linker-spec.md: No such file or directory (os error 2)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:123:10. Eleven additional refusals (section 4.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:273: :obligations-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:274: :definitions-fn      (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:275: :applications-fn     (fn [value] records)           ; step 5a, below\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:314:  format's order (step 5a). For the AST record all three scanners are\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:333:  conservative degradation of step 5a: every occurrence is retained\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:371:5a.              obligations <- join free names with declarations\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:439:   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* Two scans run over the verified\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:580:| `:use-before-definition`| 5a     | a main-sequence occurrence precedes      |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:582:| `:undeclared-free`      | 5a     | a free name has no declaration in the    |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:625:the section 4.5 query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, implemented as\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:898:Each link is a small state machine over the six steps; steps 3 to 5a\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:955:`verify`, the pure steps 3 to 5a over values already in hand, and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:1716:  7.5.2). Together they are the declarations step 5a joins free names\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2001:criterion 5a; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2075:the same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2086:## 10. File box\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2181:       under the B0 normalizer to the same program executed locally.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2190:       4.5).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2193:       a cross-host corpus of print-stable scalars, was transitional\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2208:10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2602:|                                   | 4.1 records (4.1, 4.2 step 5a,   |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2647:|                                   | 4.2 step 5a).                     |\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2681:|                                   | `validated` (4.1, 4.2